classDiagram
    %% PetTask below stands for the tuple (Pet, Task) that Owner and Scheduler pass around.

    class Task {
        <<dataclass>>
        +str description
        +str time
        +date due_date
        +str frequency
        +int duration_minutes
        +str priority
        +bool completed
        +mark_complete() Task
    }

    class Pet {
        <<dataclass>>
        +str name
        +str species
        +list~Task~ tasks
        +add_task(task) None
        +remove_task(task) None
    }

    class Owner {
        <<dataclass>>
        +str name
        +list~Pet~ pets
        +add_pet(pet) None
        +get_all_tasks() list~PetTask~
    }

    class Scheduler {
        +Owner owner
        +get_todays_schedule() list~PetTask~
        +sort_by_time(entries) list~PetTask~
        +filter_tasks(pet_name, completed) list~PetTask~
        +mark_task_complete(pet, task) Task
        +detect_conflicts() list~str~
    }

    Owner "1" o-- "*" Pet : has
    Pet "1" o-- "*" Task : has
    Scheduler --> Owner : reads tasks through
    Scheduler ..> Pet : receives with each task
    Task ..> Task : mark_complete() creates next occurrence
